Blackdrift: Gecko Remote Settings never downloads Mozilla's experiment and messaging collections.

Why: on first launch GeckoView's Remote Settings client has no local data
for most collections, so the first client that reads one calls
RemoteSettings.pullStartupBundle(). That downloads
bundles/startup.json.mozlz4 from the attachments CDN, imports every
changeset in it into the local database and registers a client for each,
so every later poll keeps them all in sync. The bundle is built for desktop
Firefox: besides lists Blackdrift uses (tracking protection, URL-classifier
exceptions, fingerprinting overrides, query stripping, DoH), it carries
nimbus-desktop-experiments, nimbus-secure-experiments, message-groups, cfr,
normandy-recipes-capabilities and newtab-wallpapers-v2. Nothing in Blackdrift
reads those (GeckoView never calls ExperimentAPI.init(), and there is no
ASRouter or Normandy), but downloading them is still contact with Mozilla's
experiment service, which Blackdrift promises not to make. Patch
focus-android/0101 only stops the app-side Nimbus fetch.

Two changes in services/settings/remote-settings.sys.mjs:

- pullStartupBundle() pulls nothing. Its only caller, a client whose
  database is empty, then syncs that one collection by itself (upstream's
  own fallback for collections missing from the bundle). The collections
  Blackdrift reads still arrive, one request each, and the experiment records are
  never downloaded.
- the poll's client lookup skips a fixed list of experiment and messaging
  collections, so a database written by an earlier Blackdrift build (which
  imported them from the bundle) is never synced again.

Remote Settings itself stays on, and every other collection is handled as
before. The file is JavaScript packaged into omni.ja, which the artifact
build stages from the local tree, so the change ships without compiled
code.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/services/settings/remote-settings.sys.mjs b/services/settings/remote-settings.sys.mjs
index b180cfc850ee..02549bc3fe25 100644
--- a/services/settings/remote-settings.sys.mjs
+++ b/services/settings/remote-settings.sys.mjs
@@ -48,6 +48,23 @@ const SIGNERS_BY_BUCKET = {
   // This is very (very) unlikely though.
 };
 
+// Blackdrift: no startup changesets bundle (see pullStartupBundle).
+const BLACKDRIFT_PULL_STARTUP_BUNDLE = false;
+
+// Blackdrift: Mozilla experiment and messaging collections. Blackdrift runs no Gecko
+// Nimbus, Normandy or messaging system, so the poll never syncs these, even
+// when a database from an earlier Blackdrift build still holds them.
+const BLACKDRIFT_SKIPPED_COLLECTIONS = new Set([
+  "cfr",
+  "message-groups",
+  "newtab-wallpapers-v2",
+  "nimbus-desktop-experiments",
+  "nimbus-mobile-experiments",
+  "nimbus-preview",
+  "nimbus-secure-experiments",
+  "normandy-recipes-capabilities",
+]);
+
 ChromeUtils.defineLazyGetter(lazy, "gPrefs", () => {
   return Services.prefs.getBranch(PREF_SETTINGS_BRANCH);
 });
@@ -186,6 +203,10 @@ function remoteSettingsFunction() {
    * with default options if possible, or `null` if bucket/collection are unknown.
    */
   async function _client(bucketName, collectionName) {
+    if (BLACKDRIFT_SKIPPED_COLLECTIONS.has(collectionName)) {
+      lazy.console.debug(`Blackdrift: not syncing ${bucketName}/${collectionName}`);
+      return null;
+    }
     // Check if a client was registered for this bucket/collection. Potentially
     // with some specific options like signer, filter function etc.
     const client = _clients.get(collectionName);
@@ -256,7 +277,10 @@ function remoteSettingsFunction() {
    * @throws {Error} If the signature of any bundled changeset is invalid.
    */
   remoteSettings.pullStartupBundle = async () => {
-    if (lazy.Utils.shouldSkipRemoteActivity) {
+    // Blackdrift: the startup bundle is built for desktop Firefox and carries the
+    // experiment and messaging collections. Pull nothing, so each collection
+    // Blackdrift reads is synced on its own (the caller's fallback).
+    if (!BLACKDRIFT_PULL_STARTUP_BUNDLE || lazy.Utils.shouldSkipRemoteActivity) {
       return [];
     }
 
